	"bugClass": {
		"id": "first-start-gate-on-continuation",
		"title": "First-start date gate blocks previously started work",
		"cause": "A due-date check intended to control the first unattended start also governs continuation. When the due date is still in the future, the shared gate can reject a replacement process restoring a checkpoint or prevent an already-started live session from reopening after an answer.",
		"criteria": "Match either a checkpoint or reboot recovery path that cannot relaunch previously started work, or a post-answer path that cannot reopen its already-started live session. Trace the continuation through the request, queue, claim, host-start, or resume logic and identify the first-start date predicate that rejects or suppresses it. Verify ownership and a prior start for the same execution using a persisted start timestamp, a recorded start event, or a checkpoint linked to a started execution. A claim, retry count, answer, or resume label alone is insufficient. Untouched future-due work and retries that have never started still belong behind the first-start gate.",
